  <knowledge>
    - show-memory ownership: commands initially belong to the AI that loaded them; ownership
  transfers to the AI that last processed or attempted to write the cell; AI-bomb classification
  updates accordingly; attempted writes count as processing even if the cell's entries remain
  unchanged.
    - show-memory selects symbols by priority: (1) next AI command of the next AI, (2) next AI
  command of other AIs, (3) AI-bomb, (4) AI command of an AI, (5) untouched since start.
    - The online submission system enforces Checkstyle and will assign zero points for violations of
   specially marked mandatory Checkstyle rules.
    - Comments should be written consistently in either English or German.
    - show-memory range display inserts the area-boundary symbol between two command symbols,
  increasing the display length by 2 * (length of the boundary symbol), then prints 10 memory cells
  per line starting at the specified cell in the format '[Symbol] [Index]: [AI-Command] | [Entry A]
  | [Entry B]' with columns right-justified and all special characters (including spaces) preserved.
    - Mandatory tests are executed before other tests; other tests are evaluated only if mandatory
  tests pass.
    - AI names provided to add-ai must not contain spaces.
    - Violation of any of the mandatory rules causes the submission to be graded with zero points.
    - Integer overflows and underflows are allowed and must wrap according to the representable
  range (for example, adding 1 to the maximum yields INT_MIN).
    - For error output the program may optionally use System.err instead of System.out.
    - Error messages must begin with 'Error,' and must not contain special characters such as
  newlines or umlauts.
    - add-ai must not overwrite an existing AI identified by name.
    - remove-ai must not remove a non-existing AI.
    - The INIT_MODE_RANDOM initialization mode requires the parameter `Seed` to initialize the
  random number generator.
  </knowledge>
