    - task.md defines the game-phase execution rules: each turn executes exactly one KI command; a
  round ends when all KIs that can act have executed; execution order is fixed by initial positions
  (KI 0, KI 1, ...); KIs do not run in parallel; executing STOP removes a KI from further execution;
   the last remaining KI 'dominates' but may still execute commands.
    - task.md defines the Code Fight memory (Speicher) as a cyclic array of numbered cells starting
