  stores a KI command and two entries (A and B).
    - ProgrammingWT2324-Final1 defines KIs as programs: a sequence of at least one KI command;
  execution proceeds to the next memory cell by default unless a KI command changes the next
  executed cell.
    - ProgrammingWT2324-Final1 simulates multiple KI programs running in a shared memory using a
  sequential, round-based execution model.
    - ProgrammingWT2324-Final1 provides the KI commands STOP, MOV_R, MOV_I, ADD, ADD_R, JMP, JMZ,
  CMP, and SWAP with the semantics summarized in section 2.3 (e.g., STOP stops execution;
  MOV_R/MOV_I copy cells; ADD/ADD_R perform additions; JMP/JMZ alter next cell; CMP can skip the
  next command; SWAP exchanges entries).
    - ProgrammingWT2324-Final1 constrains KI instruction arguments to integers in [INT_MIN, INT_MAX]
   and explicitly allows overflow/underflow (wrap-around semantics).
    - task.md defines two memory initialization modes: INIT_MODE_RANDOM and INIT_MODE_STOP
